WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Democrat parents
get this issue

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.204
as well as Republican parents.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:07.007
This is an issue that
actually unites parents

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.541
across the board.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.943
In South Carolina,

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:13.346 align:start position:0%
they were stunned by the
developments across the country

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
as it relates to
your ability to have

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.983
a gender identity group

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.820 align:start size:97% position:3%
and to have teachers
feeling like they're forced

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.722
to provide instruction.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:26.259
That is just antithetical to
what's in the best interest

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.929
of a child, to exclude the
parent from any conversation

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.165
around those very
important topics.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:36.369
And so this legislation would
pull money away from schools

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.371
who refuse to comply
with what the law,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.007
by the way, of the
land already is.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
Minors don't make
decisions in a vacuum.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
It requires a parental
supervision to make
those decisions.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.982
I have to reinforce that
by pulling the money away

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.917
so that we can make
them pay attention

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:53.586
to what the law of
the land already is.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.122
(mellow music)

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining
me today is a senator

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:04.330
from South Carolina,

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.067 align:start size:84% position:16%
as well as the author
of the new book,

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.536
"America, A Redemption Story,

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:13.273
"Choosing Hope, Creating
Unity," Senator Tim Scott.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.141
Finally, welcome to
the Rubin Report.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.242
- Well, thank you, David.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.477
It's good to be with you.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
Thank you very
much for having me.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.113
I look forward to
our conversation.

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.548
We have lots to talk about,

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:25.518 align:start position:0%
but the good news is I'm excited
to finally be on the show.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.820
Thanks for having me.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.888
- (laughs) Well,
it goes both ways.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.191
We've been trying to get
you on for quite some time.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.326
The schedules haven't quite
matched up, but here we are.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.727
So let's dive right into it.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.962
- Yes, sir.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.430 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Because I wanna
talk about the book,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.898 align:start position:0%
but I obviously wanna talk about
current events and election

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all of that
stuff, and you know,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:44.070
some of the things you're
doing right now, but first,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:48.341
the general point of
the book is positivity.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.742
It is decency.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
It is something that
seemingly everyone talks about

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.514 align:start size:81% position:19%
but nobody does
particularly well.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:55.615
I include myself in that.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.117
Sometimes I try to do it.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.651
I often fail.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.920
Can you talk a little bit
about how your life led you

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.590
to writing something
based in that idea?

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.058
- You know, Dave,

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:97% position:3%
the "America Redemption
Story" is a book that I see

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:10.530
as a positive view of
the world as it is,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.699
not as I hope that it will be.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:15.001
The truth is that what I
learned through life is

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:18.571
that the pain that I've gone
through has helped to clarify

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:22.475
my purpose, that my obstacles
have become the opportunities,

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.777 align:start size:84% position:16%
and frankly, the mess
I made of my life

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.246
has become my message.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the truth is that,
yes, it's a positive book,

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.784
but it's not one of
those pie in the sky,

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.887
hoping that something will
be different than it is.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.955
It's the reality of what is.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.926 align:start size:97% position:3%
There is a way for us to
bring forth a positive message

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.262
in the midst of the
chaos, and frankly,

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm sure we'll talk
about inflation

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.132 align:start size:97% position:3%
and some of the other
challenges that we see today.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.668 align:start size:88% position:13%
As a kid who grew up
during the Carter years,

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.437
I thank God Almighty
for Ronald Reagan.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:55.175
And so the truth is
that I learned why

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.644
I love President Ronald Reagan,

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:01.281
because of the misery
of high inflation,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:05.785 align:start size:97% position:3%
even higher interest rates,
and scarcity, not a mentality,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.287
but at the gas pump.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:10.190
So the truth is that when I
think about the hardest times

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.758
I've seen in my life,

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:16.763
somehow, some way a silver
lining appeared and that book

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.832 align:start size:88% position:13%
talks about that
silver lining and race.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.001
It talks about it with
the former president.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
It talks about it in winning
and losing elections.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:28.274
It talks about it through
this economic challenge

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.475
that we're going
through right now.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.911
So I find the silver
lining when it's there.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.379
When it's not there,

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just tell the blunt
truth that it's not there.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.851
- So, it can be tough to
find the silver lining

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
with so many of the
things going on right now

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
between inflation and
supply chain and the war,

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.458
not war in Ukraine and a
whole bunch of other stuff.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.993
But do you think,

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:49.495
do you really view us in that
Jimmy Carter moment right now,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.065
which maybe could
cause, you know,

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.833 align:start size:84% position:16%
sort of a red
pilling of Americans,

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.768
the average American
that didn't realize

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.403 align:start size:88% position:13%
that maybe big
government doesn't work

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.973
and printed money doesn't
work and the rest of it?

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.008 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, Dave, A, you're
right. (chuckles)

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.010
Big government has not worked.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.313
And we have a history to
prove that it doesn't work.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:12.318
Inflation is led by this one
concept that you talked about,

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.356
spending money you don't have,
buying things you don't need.

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:17.624
How do we prove that?

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:21.394
Well, $1.9 trillion on
a COVID relief package

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:24.864
with 1% for COVID vaccines,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:28.968
that led to pouring
literal gasoline,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:32.238 align:start size:97% position:3%
not literal, figurative
gasoline on the fire, right?

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.740
- Give them some time

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.842
when they're getting rid
of our strategic reserves.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.878 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And then you go $1.2
trillion after that

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:43.716
in an infrastructure bill that
had 10% for roads and bridges

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.918
over the next five years.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:50.923 align:start size:88% position:13%
You follow that up with
a $739 billion plan

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:57.463
called Inflation Reduction Act.

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.733 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's really the
Inflation Acceleration Act.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:04.070
And not only does it
accelerate inflation,

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:09.075
but it actually adds more fuel
to the fire by having the IRS

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.045
comb through your
file so to speak,

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:15.682 align:start size:84% position:16%
targeting people
under $200,000 a year.

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:19.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
So the truth is this is
like the Jimmy Carter years

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:24.190
in that gas is high,
inflation is high,

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.292
and interest is creeping up.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:29.829 align:start position:0%
And that's a problem that
causes a recession when combined

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the overspending
in Washington.

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:36.302 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So any time I have
a Republican on,
congressman, senator,

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:40.039
doesn't matter, I basically
ask one question always,

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:43.810
which is, do you think they
are doing this intentionally?

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:47.013
Do you believe that they
think this stuff works?

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.481
Or is this, you know,

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.750
what people are calling sort
of like a calculated implosion,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.684
something like that?

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.885
- Dave, that's a great question.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:57.657
I can't say that the
rank and file Democrats

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:03.396 align:start size:88% position:13%
have a strategy to have
the economy implode

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
because of the
pressure of inflation,

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.866
the pressure of interest rates.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:11.804
What I can tell you is that
the strategy to slow roll

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:16.042
interest rate increases had a
lot to do from my perspective

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.644
of people being up
for reappointment.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.280
It had something to do
with trying to satisfy

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.050
the whims and the wishes of
the Biden administration,

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:27.620 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that combination,
whether intentional or not,

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:31.691
led to an acceleration
of inflation in a way

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:34.527
that we haven't seen
since the Carter years.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:38.398
So I don't imagine that
they have a grand design

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:41.367
to completely destroy
the American economy.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:46.372
I do think they have a grand
design to change the very DNA

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.341
of the American people.

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:49.942
When you look at
what's happening,

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:53.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's undeniable that
what is clearly happening

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.584 align:start position:0%
is this centralization in
decision making and in spending.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.820
When you take the power and
the money and you put them

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:04.323
in the same place, that is
by design and that is bad

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:07.160 align:start size:84% position:16%
for everybody
outside the beltway.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:09.862
- So when you talk to,

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:12.598
or if you talk to say
a Democrat governor,

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.700
maybe I just fled California,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.636 align:start size:84% position:16%
now I live in the
free state of Florida.

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:17.804
- Yes.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.338 align:start size:84% position:16%
- If you were to
talk to Gavin Newsom,

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:20.773
or if you have talked to him
or just one of the Democrats

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
who show up in New York,
Whitmer, whoever it might be,

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, do they think what
they're doing is good?

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, putting aside whether
it works or not, I mean,

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:29.882
just the intention.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:32.051
I'm still unclear on this.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:33.519
I just can't figure it out.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:37.690
- Well, Dave, I have to hope
that their intentions are good.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.525
I don't know the
mind of the person

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.394
so I try my best not to decide

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:43.095 align:start size:88% position:13%
whether their intentions
are good or not.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.865
But what I can tell you
is that if you're living

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:50.069
in California or Illinois,
let me say it this way, Dave.

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:53.873
In the words of the CEO of
McDonald's headquartered

00:07:53.873 --> 00:07:57.477
in Illinois, they
are very concerned,

00:07:57.477 --> 00:08:00.947
not just with the taxes,
but with the violence.

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:05.284
They literally say people are
overdosing in our restaurants,

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:08.387 align:start size:97% position:3%
that violent crime is
happening in our restaurants.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:11.290 align:start size:84% position:16%
If this is the Chicago
and the Illinois

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:16.128
that is in our future, we're
concerned that we can't stay.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:20.967
That should have reverberated
throughout all of the country

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:23.269
and specifically in Illinois.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.238
Governor Pritzker
should have said,

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:30.243 align:start size:97% position:3%
"OMG, McDonald's is now
speaking out about the crime.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.345
"McDonald's is speaking out

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.213
"about overdoses in
their restaurant.

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:37.116 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Whatever I am
doing in this state,

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:39.185
"I should apologize and quit.

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.987
"Or if I'm not going
to do those two things,

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:45.291
"apologize and do
a 180-degree turn

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:47.393
"in the opposite direction."

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:49.262
Here's what we know works.

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:53.032
We know that rule of law works.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:56.669 align:start size:97% position:3%
We know that an objective
standard for the rule of law

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.938
being applied equally works.

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:02.608 align:start size:81% position:19%
We know that no
bail doesn't work.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:06.679
We know that defunding
the police doesn't work.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:11.651
We know that creating
tribalism doesn't work.

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:14.754
So if we know these
things don't work,

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:16.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
why does Gavin
Newsom not know that?

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:19.725 align:start size:88% position:13%
Why does Governor
Pritzker not know that?

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.594 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't have an answer
for what's going

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:22.795
through their cranial cavity.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:25.865 align:start size:81% position:19%
I can tell you
it's time to stop.

00:09:25.865 --> 00:09:28.534
- Yes, and that's why I asked
you sort of the same question

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:32.071
in two ways, because when
you see 350,000 people

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.240
flee California, which is
what happened last year,

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
you'd think Gavin might
go, "I don't know.

00:09:36.175 --> 00:09:38.978
"Maybe this has something to
do with my policies, but okay."

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:42.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Toyota ran to Texas
from California.

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:45.051
I mean, Elon Musk
is now in Texas.

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:47.720
I mean, there are some
breadcrumbs being left

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.655
by some really smart people.

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.459
They should just pick them
up and see what they lead.

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:54.727
- I keep telling people,

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:57.163
I would've paid an entry
fee to get into Florida.

00:09:57.163 --> 00:09:59.565 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't wanna give that,
and now a Floridian

00:09:59.565 --> 00:10:02.635 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm okay with that idea, but
you know, it's all right.

00:10:02.635 --> 00:10:04.437
So I wanna talk about
the Protect Kids Act

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:07.006
because you are leading on this

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:09.141
from a legislative standpoint

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:11.043 align:start size:84% position:16%
related to all of
the gender nonsense.

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.745
But before we do that,

00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:14.413
let's do one other
social justice thing.

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.816
According to my notes
here you are Black.

00:10:16.816 --> 00:10:18.017
Is that correct?

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:18.818
- My mother and my
father have confirmed

00:10:18.818 --> 00:10:20.052
the fact, I am Black.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.923 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, well, but wait
a minute, Senator.

00:10:23.923 --> 00:10:25.625
According to mainstream media,

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.226 align:start size:81% position:19%
you can't be Black
and Republican.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:28.461
What's going on here?

00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:29.929
- I have tried to
figure that out.

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:31.330 align:start size:97% position:3%
I looked at the polling
information and the polling

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.933
suggested there's 82%
chance that I'm Black,

00:10:33.933 --> 00:10:35.801
but the chances are 100%.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:39.171
Here's what's happening, and
Dave, this is really simple.

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:43.175
Any time an African American
who happens to be conservative

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.878 align:start size:84% position:16%
starts making
common sense on TV,

00:10:45.878 --> 00:10:49.949
the left must nullify the
very existence of someone

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:52.652 align:start size:84% position:16%
they wish was a
unicorn, but I am not.

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:53.552
I am real.

00:10:53.552 --> 00:10:54.787
I am not a fairytale.

