00:21:08.267 --> 00:21:10.035
enough nicks and bruises

00:21:10.035 --> 00:21:12.671
to look back and help
those who are coming

00:21:12.671 --> 00:21:15.173
and to look forward and to
know what we should take

00:21:15.173 --> 00:21:17.743
from our parents and what
we left on the sidelines.

00:21:17.743 --> 00:21:20.512
So I think we are in
the perfect age range

00:21:20.512 --> 00:21:25.517 align:start position:0%
to help recalibrate this
country for its best output yet.

00:21:26.685 --> 00:21:28.587
- What do you make
of the general thing

00:21:28.587 --> 00:21:30.088
that's happening
across the country,

00:21:30.088 --> 00:21:32.491
which is that the states
really do seem to be going

00:21:32.491 --> 00:21:34.092
in very different directions?

00:21:34.092 --> 00:21:36.328
I mean, I feel like I live in
a different country, honestly.

00:21:36.328 --> 00:21:37.496
I don't mean that
to be hyperbolic.

00:21:37.496 --> 00:21:38.897 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, from
California to Florida,

00:21:38.897 --> 00:21:41.233 align:start position:0%
you move from almost a different
country, it seems like.

00:21:41.233 --> 00:21:44.169
- I mean, literally,
3,000 miles, but truly,

00:21:44.169 --> 00:21:45.704 align:start size:81% position:19%
it feels like a
different country.

00:21:45.704 --> 00:21:47.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
Obviously, if you live
in South Carolina,

00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:49.775 align:start position:0%
that's gonna feel very different
than living in New York.

00:21:49.775 --> 00:21:51.710
COVID exacerbate a lot of that.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:55.147 align:start size:84% position:16%
Are you generally okay
with that concept?

00:21:55.147 --> 00:21:56.615
- Well, listen.

00:21:56.615 --> 00:22:00.786 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think we've had very
unique and interesting times

00:22:00.786 --> 00:22:05.424
in American history where
the states felt a tension

00:22:05.424 --> 00:22:09.795 align:start size:97% position:3%
that sometimes was not healthy
and that we overcame that.

00:22:09.795 --> 00:22:12.297 align:start size:97% position:3%
I do think we're in another
one of those moments

00:22:12.297 --> 00:22:14.766
where we're seeing the states

00:22:14.766 --> 00:22:17.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
divide amongst
themselves naturally.

00:22:17.969 --> 00:22:20.839
I mean, the good news
is when you can work

00:22:20.839 --> 00:22:22.307
and live where you want to,

00:22:22.307 --> 00:22:25.644 align:start size:88% position:13%
you move from California
to Florida, you know,

00:22:25.644 --> 00:22:28.380
or you should have stopped
by the way in South Carolina

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.848
and called it home.

00:22:29.848 --> 00:22:31.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
We say those folks who
moved from like New Jersey

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:35.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
to Florida, and then they
come back to South Carolina,

00:22:35.187 --> 00:22:36.755
that's what typically
happens over time,

00:22:36.755 --> 00:22:38.690
we call those folks half backs.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:40.559
They went all the way down.
They went all the way down.

00:22:40.559 --> 00:22:41.593
They came halfway back.

00:22:41.593 --> 00:22:43.195
So Charleston will be your home.

00:22:43.195 --> 00:22:44.863
- Nikki Haley did
a number on me too.

00:22:44.863 --> 00:22:46.365
It was on the list.

00:22:46.365 --> 00:22:47.632
It was on the list.

00:22:47.632 --> 00:22:49.267
Honestly, I have
family in Florida

00:22:49.267 --> 00:22:50.535
and that really was
like the final step.

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:52.003
- They can move up
South Carolina too.

00:22:52.003 --> 00:22:53.238
No problem.

00:22:53.238 --> 00:22:55.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have room for
your family as well.

00:22:55.273 --> 00:22:56.541
We like red voting cards.

00:22:56.541 --> 00:22:57.709
They're good.

00:22:57.709 --> 00:22:58.977 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I am a newly
registered Republican

00:22:58.977 --> 00:23:00.779 align:start size:88% position:13%
for the first time in
my life at 46 years old.

00:23:00.779 --> 00:23:01.947
- I love it.

00:23:01.947 --> 00:23:03.648 align:start size:84% position:16%
- All right, so
let's do a little bit

00:23:03.648 --> 00:23:05.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
of projecting
going forward here.

00:23:05.984 --> 00:23:07.986 align:start size:88% position:13%
Obviously these midterms
are coming, you know,

00:23:07.986 --> 00:23:09.454
most conventional thinking

00:23:09.454 --> 00:23:11.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
is there's gonna be
some kind of red wave.

00:23:11.156 --> 00:23:15.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
The incumbent party never does
that well in the midterms.

00:23:15.026 --> 00:23:16.595
What do you think
is gonna happen?

00:23:16.595 --> 00:23:18.230
What do you want to happen?

00:23:19.765 --> 00:23:23.068 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, if I had my brothers,
we would win the Senate

00:23:23.068 --> 00:23:26.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
with about two or
three seats to spare.

00:23:26.438 --> 00:23:29.007 align:start size:97% position:3%
We would have the House
with about, and when I came

00:23:29.007 --> 00:23:30.776
into the House in 2010,

00:23:30.776 --> 00:23:35.781
I think we had 63 new
seats in the House.

00:23:36.948 --> 00:23:38.583
That was a banner year,
without any question.

00:23:38.583 --> 00:23:42.721
If I had it my way, we'd have
that kind of a red tsunami.

00:23:42.721 --> 00:23:44.523
What I think is gonna happen,

00:23:44.523 --> 00:23:46.558
I think we will
control the House

00:23:46.558 --> 00:23:50.262
at the end of this election
and there is a decent chance

00:23:50.262 --> 00:23:52.397
that we can control
the Senate as well.

00:23:52.397 --> 00:23:54.533
We need to execute on the field.

00:23:54.533 --> 00:23:57.803
The game is coming down
to the last two minutes.

00:23:57.803 --> 00:24:01.173
The score's gonna be close to
tied, and I wanna make sure

00:24:01.173 --> 00:24:03.341
that when you give the
ball as a quarterback,

00:24:03.341 --> 00:24:05.277
you turn and you give your
ball to your running back.

00:24:05.277 --> 00:24:07.646 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm hoping that
Herschel will be jumping

00:24:07.646 --> 00:24:12.284
over the goal line in the
air with the ball secured,

00:24:12.284 --> 00:24:14.886 align:start size:81% position:19%
no fumbles, and
wins back Georgia.

00:24:14.886 --> 00:24:17.923 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I'm very confident
that Ted Budd

00:24:17.923 --> 00:24:20.091
will do a four and out and score

00:24:20.091 --> 00:24:22.093
on his two-minute
drills out there,

00:24:22.093 --> 00:24:25.096
and I'm hoping that Dr. Oz will
be the coach on the sideline

00:24:25.096 --> 00:24:27.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
and drawing up the
play and will execute.

00:24:27.666 --> 00:24:29.134
He was the Harvard quarterback.

00:24:29.134 --> 00:24:32.838
So maybe he'll scramble to
the left and hit the receiver

00:24:32.838 --> 00:24:34.105
for a three yard score.

00:24:34.105 --> 00:24:36.007
And then J. D. Vance, I
know he's a good author,

00:24:36.007 --> 00:24:37.209
so I'm not sure if
he plays football,

00:24:37.209 --> 00:24:38.710
but he can kick the extra point.

00:24:38.710 --> 00:24:40.312 align:start size:81% position:19%
Heck, fire him
and win that race.

00:24:40.312 --> 00:24:42.280
- I gotta tell ya, I'm
more of a basketball guy,

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:43.648
but the references
are all working.

00:24:43.648 --> 00:24:44.783
I'm following.

00:24:44.783 --> 00:24:46.017
- Good, good.

00:24:46.017 --> 00:24:47.552
I'm about done because
I started with Herschel.

00:24:47.552 --> 00:24:49.087
I know nothing about basketball,

00:24:49.087 --> 00:24:52.157
but maybe we can just get J.
D. Vance in to dunk the ball

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:53.492
after someone else spikes it.

00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:54.860
I'm sure you don't
spike the basketball.

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:56.628
- You don't spike a basketball.

00:24:56.628 --> 00:24:57.829
All right, okay.

00:24:57.829 --> 00:24:59.297
So if that happens,

00:24:59.297 --> 00:25:01.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
let's say you get something
close to what you want,

00:25:01.066 --> 00:25:05.237
even if it's not that
three senators over,

00:25:05.237 --> 00:25:07.439
et cetera, but you
get some of that.

00:25:07.439 --> 00:25:08.707
What do you think changes here?

00:25:08.707 --> 00:25:10.308
What do you think
honestly changes?

00:25:11.409 --> 00:25:13.078 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, the first thing
that should change

00:25:13.078 --> 00:25:17.949
if we control both houses
is that we start oversight,

00:25:17.949 --> 00:25:22.320 align:start size:84% position:16%
an oversight
objective to reign in

00:25:22.320 --> 00:25:26.391
this very unwieldy
group of Democrats

00:25:26.391 --> 00:25:29.294
running this country in
the Biden administration.

00:25:29.294 --> 00:25:32.931
They need oversight like a
three-year-old needs a parent

00:25:32.931 --> 00:25:34.132
to say, "Don't do this."

00:25:34.132 --> 00:25:35.567
I mean, literally we need

00:25:35.567 --> 00:25:37.669 align:start size:84% position:16%
to bring the
oversight hammer down.

00:25:37.669 --> 00:25:40.972
Number two, we have to
be the party of parents.

00:25:40.972 --> 00:25:44.609
The one thing that is manifest
today throughout this country

00:25:44.609 --> 00:25:47.112 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that school choice
and parental involvement

00:25:47.112 --> 00:25:49.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
is now more important than
it's ever been before.

00:25:49.447 --> 00:25:54.185 align:start position:0%
I think it is 67% of Democrats,
68% of the Independents,

00:25:54.185 --> 00:25:57.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
70% of African Americans,
74% of Hispanics,

00:25:57.622 --> 00:26:00.091
80% of dual-income
working families,

00:26:00.091 --> 00:26:02.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
all support some form
of school choice.

00:26:02.661 --> 00:26:05.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
After looking at the
devastating learning loss

00:26:05.830 --> 00:26:08.567 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the precipitous
drop in scores,

00:26:09.701 --> 00:26:13.605
we have to lead for parents.

00:26:13.605 --> 00:26:14.839
That's the second
thing we should do.

00:26:14.839 --> 00:26:17.509
And the third thing we
have to do in my opinion

00:26:17.509 --> 00:26:20.412
is to control our
southern border

00:26:20.412 --> 00:26:22.480
and build a physical impediment.

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:24.583
It is a national security risk.

00:26:24.583 --> 00:26:26.985
It is a fentanyl and drug risk,

00:26:26.985 --> 00:26:29.821 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it is 2 1/2 million
illegal crossing

00:26:29.821 --> 00:26:31.756
in the illegal immigration risk.

00:26:31.756 --> 00:26:34.359
And finally, what is
obvious to all of us,

00:26:35.527 --> 00:26:37.896
if you just turn
the spending off,

00:26:37.896 --> 00:26:42.000 align:start size:97% position:3%
I believe inflation comes down
in a real and manifest way.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:46.504
If you start talking about
tax policy that makes sense

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:50.108
and predictability in
the regulatory state,

00:26:50.108 --> 00:26:52.510
people with certainty
and predictability,

00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:54.112
they go back to creating jobs.

00:26:54.112 --> 00:26:55.914
They go back to making sure

00:26:55.914 --> 00:26:58.016 align:start size:84% position:16%
that they're making
long-term investments.

00:26:58.016 --> 00:27:01.252
That helps to spur the
economic engines in a way

00:27:01.252 --> 00:27:03.488 align:start size:81% position:19%
that attracts jobs
back to America

00:27:03.488 --> 00:27:04.923
and high-tech manufacturing

00:27:04.923 --> 00:27:07.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the STEM future
becomes ours.

00:27:07.626 --> 00:27:09.761
- I know that no senator
wants to be asked this,

00:27:09.761 --> 00:27:11.696
much less on their birthday,

00:27:11.696 --> 00:27:15.300 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I mean the
national ambitions,

00:27:16.534 --> 00:27:18.269
it seems like you
fit in there, man.

00:27:18.269 --> 00:27:20.939
I mean, it just seems like the
message, the tone, as I said,

00:27:20.939 --> 00:27:23.842
the age, it seems right to me.

00:27:25.410 --> 00:27:27.012
- You know, Dave,

00:27:27.012 --> 00:27:30.782 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'll tell you my
national ambition is
to travel this country

00:27:30.782 --> 00:27:35.020
for the next seven weeks and
my home state in order to win

00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:36.721
the majorities in the
House and the Senate.

00:27:36.721 --> 00:27:40.992
I am a guy that, I figured out
one thing several years ago.

00:27:40.992 --> 00:27:44.229
Applying for jobs is the
worst way to get a job.

00:27:44.229 --> 00:27:46.598
The best way to get a
job is to do that job

00:27:46.598 --> 00:27:48.199 align:start size:81% position:19%
like no one's ever
done it before,

00:27:48.199 --> 00:27:49.801
and that's one of
the reasons why

00:27:49.801 --> 00:27:51.436
in the last three weeks or so,

00:27:51.436 --> 00:27:54.439
I've been to Florence and
Myrtle Beach and Columbia

00:27:54.439 --> 00:27:57.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Charleston and
Anderson, South Carolina,

00:27:57.175 --> 00:27:58.710
as well as Rock Hill.

00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:01.179
And I'll be in Greenville and
Spartanburg and Columbia again

00:28:01.179 --> 00:28:02.113
in the next couple weeks.

00:28:02.113 --> 00:28:05.417
But I'm also in Iowa, Nebraska,

00:28:05.417 --> 00:28:10.422 align:start size:97% position:3%
Wisconsin, Michigan,
Tennessee, Florida, Georgia,

00:28:11.589 --> 00:28:13.091 align:start size:88% position:13%
and North Carolina in
the last just few weeks.

00:28:13.091 --> 00:28:14.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'll do more of the
same in the next few weeks

00:28:14.759 --> 00:28:18.797
because I believe that
the most important thing

00:28:18.797 --> 00:28:21.966
I can do with my time
and my good health

00:28:21.966 --> 00:28:24.169
is to invest it in
the future of America

00:28:24.169 --> 00:28:26.004 align:start size:81% position:19%
because one day
there will be kids

00:28:26.004 --> 00:28:28.606
like yours running this country,

00:28:28.606 --> 00:28:32.077
and we need to make
sure they start off

00:28:32.077 --> 00:28:34.913
looking at the city on the hill.

00:28:34.913 --> 00:28:36.481
That doesn't happen on accident.

00:28:36.481 --> 00:28:39.350 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think for the last
few years we thought it did.

00:28:39.350 --> 00:28:42.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Is that the sort of scariest
part of what's going on,

00:28:42.187 --> 00:28:44.022
that we seemingly have given up

00:28:44.022 --> 00:28:46.458
just what that flag right
behind you represents?

00:28:46.458 --> 00:28:47.659
Just almost like that.

00:28:47.659 --> 00:28:48.927
- Absolutely.

00:28:48.927 --> 00:28:50.428
- I know we do and the
people watching this,

00:28:50.428 --> 00:28:53.565 align:start size:97% position:3%
but so much of the ethos of
America seems to have given up

00:28:53.565 --> 00:28:55.800
on that dream and that
aspirational message.

00:28:57.702 --> 00:28:59.204
- There's something about,

00:28:59.204 --> 00:29:01.039 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I don't mean this to be
negative and I don't mean this

00:29:01.039 --> 00:29:03.608 align:start size:88% position:13%
to be insulting, I just
mean it to be real,

00:29:03.608 --> 00:29:06.111 align:start size:84% position:16%
this concept of being
a global citizen,

00:29:06.111 --> 00:29:10.949
where everything is all merged
together is really unhealthy

00:29:10.949 --> 00:29:12.917 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the United
States of America.

00:29:12.917 --> 00:29:15.086
The thing that has
always been a part

00:29:15.086 --> 00:29:19.824
of American exceptionalism
is not standing apart only.

00:29:19.824 --> 00:29:22.060
It's standing above.

00:29:22.060 --> 00:29:26.097
It's leading the world,
not being a part of it.

00:29:26.097 --> 00:29:28.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
I want to help other
countries succeed

00:29:28.933 --> 00:29:30.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
beyond their
wildest imagination,

00:29:30.902 --> 00:29:33.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that starts by
having America succeeding

00:29:33.972 --> 00:29:36.241
beyond our wildest imagination.

00:29:36.241 --> 00:29:38.676
We are the standard.

00:29:38.676 --> 00:29:43.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
When the standard
becomes average, the
world becomes subpar.

00:29:43.414 --> 00:29:46.651
- Senator, I'm gonna let you
go, 'cause it's your birthday,

00:29:46.651 --> 00:29:49.053
and I said a half hour
and we're right there.

00:29:49.053 --> 00:29:51.222
What do you do on
your 57th birthday

00:29:51.222 --> 00:29:52.257
besides hang out
with Dave Rubin?

00:29:52.257 --> 00:29:53.691
I mean, what's going on tonight?

00:29:53.691 --> 00:29:56.795 align:start size:97% position:3%
I assume you're getting
outta the office in a minute.

00:29:56.795 --> 00:29:57.796
- You know I am.

00:29:57.796 --> 00:29:59.264
I'm gonna leave the office.

00:29:59.264 --> 00:30:00.899
I'm actually gonna go for
a little bit of a run,

00:30:00.899 --> 00:30:02.066
and then I'm gonna have dinner

00:30:02.066 --> 00:30:04.869
and contemplate of the future.

00:30:04.869 --> 00:30:08.807
I love just doing goal setting.

00:30:08.807 --> 00:30:11.309 align:start size:88% position:13%
I did it before I became
a member of Congress.

00:30:11.309 --> 00:30:13.011
It's one of the things
I do on my birthday.

00:30:13.011 --> 00:30:15.880 align:start size:88% position:13%
I love just thinking
about the next 12 months

00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:19.450 align:start size:97% position:3%
and how to make my 50s
fabulous, and a part of that,

00:30:19.450 --> 00:30:22.387
I will decide that the
next 12 months tonight.

00:30:22.387 --> 00:30:24.255
- Senator, I hope your
predictions are right.

00:30:24.255 --> 00:30:26.057 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I'm glad we
finally got to do this.

00:30:26.057 --> 00:30:27.959
I hope we can do it
in person sometime.

00:30:27.959 --> 00:30:29.060
Happy birthday to you.

00:30:30.061 --> 00:30:30.995
- Later, Dave.

00:30:30.995 --> 00:30:32.497
God bless you.

00:30:32.497 --> 00:30:35.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
And congratulations on being
a brand brand new father,

00:30:35.033 --> 00:30:36.334
maybe again, but pretty close.

00:30:36.334 --> 00:30:38.303
- First, I'm going
to bed right now.

00:30:38.303 --> 00:30:39.270
- First one.

00:30:39.270 --> 00:30:40.672
There you go. (laughs)

00:30:40.672 --> 00:30:41.506 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Thanks.
- God bless you.

00:30:41.506 --> 00:30:42.740
- Take care.

